14:25.020 --> 14:29.220
that goes from B to E through the solid line.

14:29.220 --> 14:34.060
So this is the path, this is the solid path.

14:34.060 --> 14:42.140
Well, if this was the case, since the cost is additive, then the cost to go from A to

14:42.140 --> 14:49.300
E through C would be JAB plus JBCE.

14:49.300 --> 14:55.100
And the cost to go from A to E, and the cost of the problem to go from A to E without going

14:55.100 --> 15:02.360
through C would be JAB plus GBE.

15:02.360 --> 15:10.540
But since we are assuming by contradiction that JBCE is less than JBE, then let's call

15:10.540 --> 15:18.460
this the cost of path two, cost of path one, then the cost of path two will be less than

15:18.460 --> 15:20.500
cost of path one.

15:20.500 --> 15:24.300
Which is a contradiction because we start as an assumption that the optimal way to go

15:24.300 --> 15:33.820
from A to E is not to go through C. So the contradiction stems from the fact that we

15:33.820 --> 15:43.100
assumed that indeed the optimal sequence to go from B to E is not the tail of the optimal

15:43.100 --> 15:48.740
trajectory to go from A to E. Does that make sense?

15:48.740 --> 15:52.220
So the principle of humanity is a very straightforward concept.

15:53.140 --> 15:57.340
Sometimes it's a bit deceptively simple, so it takes a little time to be internalized,

15:57.340 --> 16:00.800
