16:00.800 --> 16:06.580
So let's just pause for a second to make sure that everyone is on board with this idea.

16:06.580 --> 16:17.620
Again, we proved that the tail of an optimal sequence is optimal for the tail subproblem.

16:17.620 --> 16:23.020
To do that, we use a proof of contradiction where we say, well, assume by the second contradiction

16:23.020 --> 16:29.420
that the tail subproblem, meaning the problem of going optimally from B to E, is solved

16:29.420 --> 16:35.180
by another trajectory, which is different from the tail trajectory of the optimal sequence

