C. But if that is the case, then we would have found, because the cost is additive,

16:53.220 --> 16:58.900
a new trajectory from A that has a lower cost with respect to the one that we assume to

16:58.900 --> 17:01.540
be optimal, which is a contradiction.

17:01.540 --> 17:05.540
This proves that, indeed, the tail policy was optimal.

17:05.540 --> 17:14.300
So very simple proof.

17:14.300 --> 17:18.860
We can do it in a way that is more tailored to our discrete time framework, but the idea

17:18.860 --> 17:22.740
is exactly the same.

