01:07:34.700 --> 01:07:35.820
in a slightly different way.

01:07:35.820 --> 01:07:40.940
So there was some concern that with the previous questions,

01:07:40.940 --> 01:07:43.140
people were introducing biases.

01:07:43.140 --> 01:07:45.300
Some biases were quite surprising to me.

01:07:45.300 --> 01:07:49.980
For example, on average, classes instructed by female professors

01:07:49.980 --> 01:07:52.460
had much lower ratings.

01:07:52.460 --> 01:07:58.620
And classes instructed early morning had lower ratings.

01:07:58.620 --> 01:07:59.740
A lot of weird biases.

01:07:59.740 --> 01:08:01.860
So basically, there was a task force within the School

01:08:01.900 --> 01:08:04.620
of Engineering to change a little bit how questions

01:08:04.620 --> 01:08:06.500
are asked in order to see if there is

01:08:06.500 --> 01:08:09.100
a way to eliminate these biases.

01:08:09.100 --> 01:08:11.220
So the point being is that you have

01:08:11.220 --> 01:08:14.300
to fill out not just the standard course evaluation,

01:08:14.300 --> 01:08:17.140
but also an additional experimental course evaluation

01:08:17.140 --> 01:08:21.980
that we'll make available to you this week.

